  "rule": "Generated, not curated: a glyph superscripts iff Unicode defines a modifier letter (Lm) or superscript digit (No) whose compatibility decomposition is <super> of it. Exceptions ʔ→ˀ and ʕ→ˤ have no decomposition. Latin Extended-F forms (U+10780+, Unicode 14) are excluded — correct but near-universally tofu. One further exception: bare `g` is U+0067 for the plain-US constraint, but it stands for IPA ɡ (U+0261), so it superscripts to ᶢ (ɡ's form), not ᵍ."
